Project Development Phase
Legalease – Project Development Phase

The Project Development Phase is the stage where the design of Legalease is converted into a working software application. During this phase, the planned modules, database, user interface, AI features, and security functions are implemented and integrated.

1. Objective

The main objectives of the development phase are:

Develop the Legalease application.
Implement the designed modules.
Create and connect the database.
Develop the AI-powered legal assistant.
Implement document-generation features.
Connect users with relevant official resources.
Test individual components during development.
2. Development Process

The development can be carried out in the following order:

System Setup
     ↓
Frontend Development
     ↓
Backend Development
     ↓
Database Development
     ↓
AI Legal Assistant
     ↓
Document Generation
     ↓
Resource Integration
     ↓
Security Implementation
     ↓
Module Integration
3. Frontend Development

The frontend provides the interface through which users interact with Legalease.

Main screens
Home page
Login/Register page
User dashboard
Legal Assistant page
Legal topics page
Document generator
Resources page
User history page
Admin dashboard

Technologies such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Bootstrap, or React can be used.

4. Backend Development

The backend handles the main application logic.

It manages:

User authentication
User queries
Database operations
AI requests
Document generation
Resource management
API communication

A backend framework such as Python, Java, or Node.js can be used.

5. Database Development

A MySQL or PostgreSQL database can be created to store:

User accounts
Legal topics
Legal information
User questions
AI responses/history
Document templates
Official resources

The database is connected to the backend through appropriate database APIs or an ORM.

6. AI Legal Assistant Development

The AI assistant is one of the main components of Legalease.

Development workflow
User Question
      ↓
Text Processing
      ↓
Identify Legal Topic
      ↓
Retrieve Verified Information
      ↓
Generate Response
      ↓
Display Answer

The assistant should preferably use a retrieval-based approach, where responses are grounded in verified legal sources rather than relying only on the model's general knowledge.

It should also provide appropriate notices such as:

“This information is for general educational purposes and is not a substitute for advice from a qualified legal professional.”

7. Document Generator Development

A document-generation module can be developed for basic templates.

Example workflow
Select Template
      ↓
Enter Required Details
      ↓
Validate Information
      ↓
Generate Document
      ↓
Preview
      ↓
Download

Possible templates include:

Complaint letters
Application letters
Consumer complaints
Basic legal notices
RTI application templates
8. Legal Resource Integration

The application can provide links to appropriate official government and legal-service websites.

Resources can be organized by category:

Consumer complaints
Cybercrime reporting
Legal aid
Court services
Government departments
Emergency services

Each resource should preferably include its source, description, and last-updated date.

9. Security Implementation

Security features include:

Password hashing
Secure authentication
Session management
Input validation
Authorization
HTTPS
Database access controls
Protection of personal information

Sensitive information should not be collected unless it is genuinely required for the feature.

10. Module Integration

After developing individual modules, they are connected into one system.

User Interface
      ↓
Backend/API
      ↓
 ┌────┼───────────┐
 ↓    ↓           ↓
DB   AI Engine   Documents
 │    │           │
 └────┴───────────┘
      ↓
Legal Resources
11. Testing During Development

Each module is tested while being developed.

Examples

User Module

Test registration.
Test login.
Test invalid credentials.

AI Assistant

Test different types of legal questions.
Check whether responses are relevant.
Verify that sources are correctly displayed.

Database

Test inserting, updating, and retrieving information.

Document Generator

Test different templates.
Check generated documents for missing or incorrect fields.
12. Development Deliverables

At the end of this phase, the project should have:

Working frontend
Functional backend
Configured database
AI legal assistant
Document-generation module
Legal resource section
Authentication system
Basic security controls
Integrated application ready for final testing
13. Conclusion

The Project Development Phase transforms the Legalease design into a functional application. The frontend, backend, database, AI assistant, document generator, and legal-resource modules are developed and integrated during this stage. After successful development, the completed system proceeds to the Testing and Evaluation Phase, where its functionality, accuracy, security, usability, and reliability are evaluated.
